From: =?UTF-8?q?Jonas=20H=C3=B6chst?= <hoechst@trackit.systems>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:06:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] huawei: keep ^HCSQ values reported unsolicited

The extended signal values are loaded by querying ^HCSQ? after clearing
the previous values, relying on the ^HCSQ handler to parse the response.
The ZOWEE E3372-325 replies to ^HCSQ? with a bare OK and only reports
^HCSQ unsolicited, so the values were always empty.

Don't clear the values before the query. The ^HCSQ handler replaces them
whenever a ^HCSQ message arrives, as response or unsolicited, so devices
that answer the query behave as before.
---
 src/plugins/huawei/mm-broadband-modem-huawei.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/huawei/mm-broadband-modem-huawei.c b/src/plugins/huawei/mm-broadband-modem-huawei.c
index f711573..09d08bf 100644
--- a/src/plugins/huawei/mm-broadband-modem-huawei.c
+++ b/src/plugins/huawei/mm-broadband-modem-huawei.c
@@ -4770,9 +4770,10 @@ signal_load_values (MMIfaceModemSignal *_self,
 
     task = g_task_new (self, cancellable, callback, user_data);
 
-    /* Clear any previous detailed signal values to get new ones */
-    detailed_signal_clear (&self->priv->detailed_signal);
-
+    /* Don't clear the previous detailed signal values: the ^HCSQ handler
+     * replaces them whenever a ^HCSQ message arrives, either as the response
+     * to this query or unsolicited. Some devices (e.g. the ZOWEE E3372-325)
+     * only send them unsolicited and reply to the query with a bare OK. */
     mm_base_modem_at_command (MM_BASE_MODEM (self),
                               "^HCSQ?",
                               3,
